  "title": "Central Government Raises MSP for Wheat and Rabi Crops",
  "summary": "The Indian government has increased the minimum support prices (MSP) for wheat and rabi crops by ₹25 per quintal, bringing the MSP to ₹2,610 per quintal for the 2027-28 rabi marketing year. The increase reflects a nominal hike based on agricultural cost factors, global and domestic price trends, and the recommendations of the Central Agricultural Cost and Prices Committee (CACP).",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Central Government has increased the MSP for wheat and rabi crops by ₹25 per quintal, bringing it to ₹2,610 per quintal for the 2027-28 rabi marketing year.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The increase was approved by the Union Cabinet, citing agricultural cost factors, global and domestic price trends, and recommendations from the Commission for Agricultural Costs & Prices.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The MSP for wheat was fixed at ₹2,585 per quintal for the 2026-27 rabi marketing year.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
